    {
      "publicId": "chal_coding_pdp_162",
      "name": "dedup-order-events",
      "type": "mini_coding",
      "title": "Load order events exactly once",
      "description": "The apps send order events at least once: a phone that misses the acknowledgement resends the same event (same `event_id`, later `ingested_at`), and an offline phone sends yesterday's events in tonight's file. The revenue report came out 6% too high, and replaying a broken night crashed the load. The editor holds `pipelines/order_events.py` with its key pieces missing, each marked by a `# [ ]` line; some pieces are wrong on purpose. Fill every line so that `load_night` keeps one row per `event_id` from the file (the copy that arrived first), adds only events the `events` table does not have yet, and can load the same file twice without changing anything or failing; and `Q_DAILY_REVENUE` sums `order_paid` amounts per business day in Ho Chi Minh City (UTC+7), whichever night the event arrived. Run loads the test's nights into SQLite and prints events per type, revenue per day and which copy of an event was kept.",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "outcomes": [
        "modeling"
      ],
      "points": 30,
      "hints": [
        "Write down what makes two rows \"the same event\". Two copies of one retry share something that two bowls of the same dish in one order do not.",
        "Look at `ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY ... ORDER BY ...)` to keep one row per key inside the file, `INSERT ... SELECT ... ON CONFLICT (...) DO NOTHING` against the primary key for copies loaded on earlier nights, and SQLite's `date(ts, '+7 hours')` for a local day.",
        "Deduplicating page views by `view_id`, keeping the first copy and counting views per local day in Bangkok (UTC+7): `SELECT * FROM (SELECT v.*, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY view_id ORDER BY received_at) AS n FROM raw_views v) WHERE n = 1`, loaded with `INSERT INTO views ... ON CONFLICT (view_id) DO NOTHING`, and reported with `SELECT date(viewed_at, '+7 hours') AS day, COUNT(*) FROM views GROUP BY day`."
      ],
      "coding": {
        "language": "python",
        "filePath": "pipelines/order_events.py",
        "executionMode": "stdio",
        "timeLimitMs": 3000,
        "memoryLimitMb": 128,
        "scoringMode": "all_or_nothing",
        "maxAttempts": null
      },
